  "notes": [
    "http_requests_total and capacity_rps have one series per job (200): A and B join them on(job) as the group_left right side, which needs one series per job.",
    "Histograms (http_request_duration_seconds_bucket, delivery_latency_bucket, calc_duration_bucket, data_latency_bucket): per sample a Zipf(1.1) number of observations in 1..20, log-normal (median 0.05, sigma 1); buckets cumulative over le.",
    "cache_hits_total <= cache_lookups_total (per-series ratio 0.5-0.99); http_errors_total = a 0-2% share of its job's http_requests_total increments.",
    "Other counters: Zipf(1.1, N=1e6) integer increments, 5% of series reset every 30-120 min; gauges: Zipf integers x an integer per-series multiplier.",
    "L5 uses MetricsQL's implicit subquery rate(label_replace(...)[1m]).",
    "L6's offset is on the selector (the same meaning as an offset after the aggregation, which is not valid PromQL). L1 and L5 run on VictoriaMetrics only (engines field); ASAP plans and answers the other 19 queries.",
    "The run is 3 h from zero; windows longer than 3h (A, B, E, L1, L2, L3: 6h) are capped at 3h; the original query text is in promql_original."
  ],
